    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d527">

                <pb facs="0789" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/8–2054</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the United Nations Adviser, Bureau of Far
                        Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bacon</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Regional Planning Adviser, Bureau of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ogburn</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-08-20">August 20, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <item>Subject:</item>
                    <item>Chinese Representation</item>
                </list>
                <p>The Secretary informed the Belgian Ambassador yesterday that we would like very
                    much to support Belgium for a Security Council post.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d527-f1"/> Indicating that there was no sense of trade involved, the
                    Secretary expressed the hope that the Belgians would continue to support our
                    position on Chinese representation. The Belgian Ambassador, without giving any
                    commitment, made assuring remarks to the general effect that Belgium had taken a
                    prominent part in the finding of aggression against the Chinese Communists and
                    that this and other matters would have to be cleared up, of course, before
                    consideration could be given to seating the Chinese Communists in the United
                    Nations.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
